Editor type mappings can now be configured from a dedicated ''Editor Types'' tab under Settings in the control panel, replacing the read-only table that previously lived under the Advanced tab. Each content type shows a dropdown of the editors available in the wiki, so installing an editor plugin (such as CodeMirror) is immediately selectable without manually editing the mapping tiddlers.

To make the dropdown reliable, content editor widget modules now export an `edit-types` array containing the editor type names they provide (for example `text`, `bitmap`, `binary`, or `codemirror`). The dropdown is populated with `[[widget]modules[]moduleproperty[edit-types]jsonget[]]`, so the JavaScript module exports are the source of truth and widgets that merely happen to share the `edit-` prefix (such as `edit-shortcut`) are not listed.
